# BuildKit reads <Dockerfile>.dockerignore (next to the Dockerfile) in preference to a
# .dockerignore at the root of the build context, so this applies to the repository-root context.
# Allowlist: send only what the image needs; never keys, certificates, virtualenvs or caches.
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!packages/
!examples/payment-transfer/payment_demo/

**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/.mypy_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
**/*.sqlite3
packages/*/tests
